  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Association's LINE Chat",
    "overview": "\n**Creative North Star: \"The Association's LINE Chat\"**\n\nFamilyLink looks and behaves like a conversation with the association inside LINE, the app its older staff and caregivers already trust. A pale blue-grey wallpaper (the chat ground) carries a white content pane; system messages are speech bubbles with a small flattened corner; people are friend-list rows with a round initial; the main sections are a rich-menu tab bar. Everything is large, soft and Thai-first: 18px body, 48px or taller targets, rounded 14px controls.\n\nGreen is the one brand voice, but it is used in two ways on purpose. Bright LINE green (#06c755) is a fill only and always carries dark ink; a deeper green (#067d34) carries text, links, focus rings and selected states, because white on LINE green fails contrast. Status is always a drawn glyph plus a Thai word on a tinted chip; colour only reinforces it. Light and dark are both first-class: the app follows the device unless a person chooses สว่าง or มืด.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Chat-bubble messages, friend-list rows, bottom tab bar: borrowed from LINE, not decoration.",
      "Two greens: bright fill with dark ink, deep green for text and focus.",
      "Soft grey (not outlines) separates secondary controls and groups.",
      "Flat surfaces; one faint ambient shadow, no floating panels.",
      "Motion is small, transform-only, and absent under reduced motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Dark Ink On Green Rule",
        "body": "Bright LINE green is a fill and takes only Green Ink text. Text, links and focus use Action Green. White-on-#06c755 is forbidden.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glyph And Word Rule",
        "body": "No status is communicated by colour alone: every state is a drawn glyph plus a Thai word.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Both Themes Rule",
        "body": "Any new colour role gets a light and a dark value under the same custom property name; never hard-code a colour in a component.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Eighteen Floor Rule",
        "body": "Nothing renders below 0.95rem (about 17px); body stays 18px.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tonal First Rule",
        "body": "Separate with soft grey or a hairline before reaching for a shadow; a shadow means the thing floats.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use bright LINE green only as a fill with Green Ink (#04210f) text; use Action Green for text, links and focus.",
      "**Do** pair every status with a glyph and a Thai word on a chip.",
      "**Do** keep targets at 48px or taller (tabs 68px, buttons 52px, inputs 56px) and body at 18px.",
      "**Do** define colours as custom properties with both a light and dark value.",
      "**Do** keep destructive actions red and worded, never the green of a save.",
      "**Do** keep motion transform-only and inside `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put white text on #06c755.",
      "**Don't** signal state with colour alone, or animate opacity.",
      "**Don't** use shadows for ordinary separation; the Sheet shadow belongs to floating panels.",
      "**Don't** add new text below 0.95rem or Latin-only labels; copy is Thai.",
      "**Don't** hard-code new pastels or hex values in components."
    ]
  }
